---
/**
 * /alerts/ — what the email alerts are, and the signup form.
 *
 * Like every page under /alerts/, it stays reachable when PUBLIC_ALERTS_API is
 * empty but explains that the feature is not enabled on this build, so a fork
 * never ships a form that silently posts nowhere.
 */
import Base from '../../components/Base.astro';
import AlertsSignup from '../../components/AlertsSignup.astro';
import { ALERTS_API, href } from '../../lib/site';

const enabled = !!ALERTS_API;
// The one alerts URL search should find, so its <title> is the query it should
// answer. /alerts/manage/ and the state pages carried this same title and
// Semrush read them as duplicates; they are noindex now (site/src/lib/seo.mjs).

---

<Base
  title="AI Workshop Deadline Email Alerts"
  description="Get email alerts for AI, machine learning, computer vision, and robotics workshop deadlines: a weekly digest, plus a warning when a saved deadline moves or is about to close. No account needed."
>
  <section class="masthead">
    <p class="eyebrow">Optional</p>
    <h1>Deadline alerts by email</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Deadline extensions, new calls, and the workshops you saved, covering only the conferences
      and topics you choose, with nothing sent in a quiet week.
    </p>
  </section>

  {!enabled && (
    <p class="muted">
      Email alerts are not enabled on this build of the site. The tracker itself works exactly the
      same without them. Everything on the <a href={href('/')}>deadline board</a> and your{' '}
      <a href={href('/saved/')}>saved list</a> is unaffected.
    </p>
  )}

  <div class="prose">
    <h2>What arrives</h2>
    <p>
      Three things, and you tick which of them you want. They are independent: take all three,
      or just one.
    </p>

    <h3>The weekly digest</h3>
    <p>Every Monday, one message with four short sections, filtered to your selection:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Your saved workshops</strong>: the next deadlines on your saved list, whatever your
        filters say, and never truncated.</li>
      <li><strong>Deadline changes this week</strong>: extensions and any date that moved earlier, grouped by conference.</li>
      <li><strong>New this week</strong>: workshops added to the tracker this week.</li>
      <li><strong>Closing in the next 7 days</strong>: sorted by whichever stage is next.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      A summary line at the top counts the week in one glance, and every change carries a small
      badge (<strong>EXTENDED +5d</strong>, <strong>DEADLINE POSTED</strong>,{' '}
      <strong>CLOSES TODAY</strong>), so what happened is the first thing you read rather than
      something buried mid-sentence. All times are UTC, stated once.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Quiet weeks send nothing.</strong> If none of your areas moved, there is no email.
      The digest is skipped rather than padded.
    </p>

    <h3>A deadline you follow is close</h3>
    <p>
      One alert when a workshop you saved is within 72 hours of closing. Sent once per deadline.
      If the organizers then extend it, the new date re-arms it.
    </p>

    <h3>A deadline you follow moved</h3>
    <p>
      One alert on the day we record a change to a saved workshop's deadline: an extension, a date
      brought forward, or a deadline published for the first time. This is the one worth having if
      you would rather not wait until Monday to hear that something slipped.
    </p>

    <h2>A sample</h2>
    <pre class="alerts-sample"><code>{`This week in AI workshops
2 deadline changes · 1 new workshop · 1 of your saved closes within 48h
Your selection, for the week ending 25 Aug 2026.

Your saved workshops — next deadlines
-------------------------------------
All times UTC.
* ★ [CLOSES TODAY] Agentic Evaluation (AGENTIC · ICML 2026) · 25 Aug 2026, 23:59

Deadline changes this week
--------------------------

ECCV
* [EXTENDED +5d] Marine Robotics and Perception (MARINE · ECCV 2026) · in 25 days · 19 Sep 2026, 23:59

NeurIPS
* [DEADLINE POSTED] AI for Accelerated Materials Design (AI4Mat · NeurIPS 2026) · in 39 days · 3 Oct 2026, 23:59

New this week
-------------
workshops added to the tracker this week
* [NEW] Safe Generative Modelling (SAFEGEN · NeurIPS 2026) · in 5 days · 30 Aug 2026, 07:59

Closing in the next 7 days
--------------------------
* ★ [CLOSES TODAY] Agentic Evaluation (AGENTIC · ICML 2026) · 25 Aug 2026, 23:59
*   Safe Generative Modelling (SAFEGEN · NeurIPS 2026) · in 5 days · 30 Aug 2026, 07:59 (abstract)

Median extension this week: 5 days.`}</code></pre>
  </div>

  <AlertsSignup
    heading="Subscribe"
    blurb="Double opt-in: you'll get one confirmation email, and nothing else until you click it."
    compact
  />

  <div class="prose">
    <h2>Questions</h2>

    <h3>Is the data guaranteed correct?</h3>
    <p>
      No, and the emails say so. Dates are when <em>we</em> recorded a value, not necessarily when
      organizers changed it, and some entries are unverified imports.{' '}
      <strong>Always confirm on the official workshop page</strong> before you plan a submission.
    </p>

    <h3>Do I need an account?</h3>
    <p>
      No. There is no password and no profile: your email address plus a signed link is the whole
      system. To change anything later, request a sign-in link on the{' '}
      <a href={href('/alerts/manage/')}>manage page</a>.
    </p>

    <h3>What do you store, and how do I delete it?</h3>
    <p>
      Your address, the conferences and topics you picked, your starred items, and your cadence.
      Nothing else: no open tracking, no click redirects, no third-party sharing. Unsubscribing{' '}
      <strong>deletes the row entirely</strong>, immediately: there is no "inactive" state to sit in.
      Every email has a one-click unsubscribe link, and the manage page has the same button.
    </p>

    <h3>Does my saved list still work without this?</h3>
    <p>
      Completely. Starring writes to your own browser and always has. Subscribing simply lets that
      list follow you to another device. See <a href={href('/saved/')}>your saved list</a>.
    </p>

    <h3>Can I just use a calendar or the RSS feed instead?</h3>
    <p>
      New workshops are announced in the <a href={href('/rss.xml')}>RSS feed</a>, and the full
      dataset is at <a href={href('/api/workshops.json')}><code>/api/workshops.json</code></a> if
      you'd rather build your own reminder.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .alerts-sample {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 1rem 1.1rem;
    overflow-x: auto;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .alerts-sample code { background: none; padding: 0; }
</style>
